---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Data Processing Addendum | Plokr" description="Plokr's Data Processing Addendum for GDPR and data protection compliance." noIndex={false}>
  <header class="phero">
    <div class="wrap-xs" style="padding:0 56px">
      <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
      <h1 style="font-size:44px">Data Processing Addendum</h1>
      <p class="lede" style="font-size:16px;margin-top:14px">Last updated April 1, 2026</p>
      <div class="legaltabs">
        <a href="/privacy">Privacy</a>
        <a href="/terms">Terms</a>
        <a href="/dpa" class="on">DPA</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>
  <article class="sec" style="padding-top:48px">
    <div class="wrap-xs">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>This Data Processing Addendum ("DPA") is incorporated into and forms part of the Plokr Terms of Service between Plokr, Inc. ("Plokr", "Processor") and the customer ("Controller"). It applies where Plokr processes personal data on your behalf subject to applicable data protection law, including the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) and UK GDPR.</p>

        <h2>1. Definitions</h2>
        <p>"Personal Data", "Controller", "Processor", "Processing", and "Data Subject" have the meanings given in applicable data protection law. "Standard Contractual Clauses" (SCCs) means the clauses issued by the European Commission under Decision 2021/914/EU.</p>

        <h2>2. Scope and role</h2>
        <p>Where Plokr processes Personal Data on your behalf to provide the service (for example, names and work email addresses of users you invite), Plokr acts as a Processor and you act as the Controller. Plokr's processing of personal data as a Controller in connection with your account (e.g., billing contact) is governed by the Privacy Policy, not this DPA.</p>

        <h2>3. Instructions</h2>
        <p>Plokr will process Personal Data only on your documented instructions, including as set out in these Terms and DPA, unless required to do so by applicable law. Plokr will inform you if, in its opinion, an instruction infringes data protection law.</p>

        <h2>4. Confidentiality</h2>
        <p>Plokr ensures that persons authorised to process Personal Data have committed to confidentiality or are under an appropriate statutory obligation of confidentiality.</p>

        <h2>5. Security</h2>
        <p>Plokr implements and maintains technical and organisational measures to protect Personal Data against accidental or unlawful destruction, loss, alteration, or unauthorised disclosure, including those described on our <a href="/security">Security page</a>: TLS 1.2+ in transit, AES-256 at rest, per-workspace token isolation, and access logging.</p>

        <h2>6. Sub-processors</h2>
        <p>You provide general authorisation for Plokr to engage sub-processors. Plokr maintains a current list of sub-processors at plokr.com/sub-processors and will provide 14 days' notice of any new sub-processor. Plokr imposes equivalent data protection obligations on all sub-processors by contract.</p>

        <h2>7. Data subject rights</h2>
        <p>Plokr will assist you, to the extent possible given the nature of processing, in responding to Data Subject requests to exercise rights under applicable data protection law (access, rectification, erasure, portability, restriction, objection). You are responsible for ensuring you have a lawful basis for Processing and for responding to Data Subjects.</p>

        <h2>8. Security incidents</h2>
        <p>Plokr will notify you without undue delay (and in any event within 72 hours of becoming aware) of any Personal Data breach affecting your data. Notification will include the information required by GDPR Article 33(3) to the extent then known. Plokr will cooperate with your investigation and remediation efforts.</p>

        <h2>9. Data protection impact assessments</h2>
        <p>Plokr will provide reasonable assistance to you in carrying out data protection impact assessments (DPIAs) and prior consultations with supervisory authorities, where required by applicable data protection law and to the extent Plokr has relevant information.</p>

        <h2>10. Deletion and return</h2>
        <p>On termination of the service or at your request, Plokr will delete or return Personal Data and delete existing copies within 30 days, except to the extent retention is required by applicable law. Plokr will certify such deletion in writing on request.</p>

        <h2>11. Audits</h2>
        <p>Plokr will make available information necessary to demonstrate compliance with this DPA and allow for and contribute to audits and inspections conducted by you or your auditor, subject to reasonable notice, confidentiality obligations, and reimbursement of Plokr's reasonable costs. SOC 2 Type II reports satisfy this obligation for annual audits.</p>

        <h2>12. International transfers</h2>
        <p>Where Plokr transfers Personal Data originating in the European Economic Area, UK, or Switzerland to a country that has not been deemed adequate, such transfers are made pursuant to the Standard Contractual Clauses (Module 2: Controller to Processor), which are incorporated herein by reference. By accepting this DPA you execute those SCCs. Plokr's data is primarily hosted in the United States.</p>

        <h2>13. Precedence</h2>
        <p>In the event of any conflict between this DPA and the Terms of Service regarding the processing of Personal Data, this DPA takes precedence.</p>

        <h2>14. Contact</h2>
        <p>For DPA-related enquiries, contact our Data Protection contact at <a href="mailto:privacy@plokr.com">privacy@plokr.com</a>. To execute a signed DPA for enterprise compliance, email <a href="mailto:legal@plokr.com">legal@plokr.com</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
